From 6b6eb735d16b47d17fe6ed2edb95a4c146081f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:44:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): scale three-finger swipe travel via
 [input.gesture] strip_travel_scale
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three-finger travel arrives pointer-accelerated, so the same physical swipe
covers more distance when the fingers move fast; the only workaround was
touchpad sensitivity, which moves the pointer speed too. strip_travel_scale
scales how far a swipe pans the scrolling strip, including strip pans inside
overview previews (1.0 keeps the upstream distances; below 1.0 a swipe covers
less ground) without touching pointer speed, window drag, or window resize.

Only viewport-pan travel scales. Workspace movement keeps fixed travel at any
scale — the desktop workspace-switch swipe and the overview's along-axis
navigation between workspaces share kSwipeWorkspacePx, so one swipe step reads
the same distance on either side of the overview. The scroll stream arrives
unaccelerated, and the four-finger overview gesture and gestures forwarded to
applications keep their fixed distances. The headless backend cannot inject
three-finger swipes, so the scale is pinned by config_load and gesture-physics
unit tests instead of a harness check.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
