diff --git a/docs/user/input.md b/docs/user/input.md
index c1e43c5f..a0959c51 100644
--- a/docs/user/input.md
+++ b/docs/user/input.md
@@ -323,6 +323,15 @@ X11 windows that declare `Input=False` without `WM_TAKE_FOCUS`, including Steam'
 
 `follows_mouse_max_scroll` limits how far Umbriel may scroll a layout to reveal that window, measured in viewport widths. `0.0` allows only fully visible windows. Omit the key for no limit.
 
+### Gestures
+
+```toml
+[input.gesture]
+strip_travel_scale = 1.0
+```
+
+`strip_travel_scale` scales how far a three-finger swipe pans the scrolling strip, including the strip pan inside overview previews. Three-finger travel arrives pointer-accelerated, so the same physical swipe covers more distance when the fingers move fast; a value below `1.0` makes a swipe cover less ground without changing pointer speed, window drag, or window resize. The value scales the finger travel one pan needs: `0.7` takes about 1.4 times the travel per viewport pan, `2.0` half. Accepted values are `0.1` to `10.0`; `1.0` keeps the built-in distances. Workspace movement keeps its existing travel at any scale — both the workspace-switch swipe and the overview's along-axis navigation between workspaces — so one swipe step reads the same distance there; the four-finger overview gesture and gestures forwarded to applications also keep their existing travel.
+
 ### Controller desktop input
 
 Steam's desktop controller mappings can control native Wayland windows through Umbriel's X11 input emulation. Umbriel asks for permission on the first request and remembers the decision for the current session. See [X11 desktop input](security.md#x11-desktop-input) for consent and lock-screen behavior.
